#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""renda-harness: the PR desk as code, with the local model (on our Omega engine) only where judgement is needed.

Drake 2026-10-20: "build it a harness", "local and fast", "on my kernels". The old renda-local let a 30B model
wander a shell for every step. Here every mechanical step is code, done in parallel per repo:

  CLEAN + Spark SUCCESS on the exact head  -> read the diff, one short review call to the local model, squash merge
                                              with --match-head-commit (one merge per repo per pass)
  Spark SUCCESS, hosted check failed       -> confirm the bundle is in aien-receipts, rerun the hosted check
  BLOCKED NOT_RUN PIPELINE_CONFIG_CHANGED  -> start the operator judge run (Drake's "merge everything" is the A4 OK),
                                              one per repo at a time, never a second judge on one sha
  DIRTY (behind main, conflicts)           -> rebase onto main (crumb-only conflicts resolved by rebase-crumb.sh),
                                              push with a lease; the Spark workers judge the new head
  Spark FAILURE / ERROR (not A4)           -> reported, never retried (a failing gate means the work is wrong)

Workers: `renda-harness --name renda1 --lanes a,b,c` (loop forever) or `--once`. One instance per name (flock).
Model: whatever 127.0.0.1:18091 serves (aien-serve-http --engine omega). If it is down, merges wait; the
mechanical steps (rebase, rerun, operator runs) carry on.
"""
